 1.1M shares, 2.00x the prior 10-day average of 561K. It didn't hold. By Jan 5, 2005 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $43.84.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}